  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Airbnb Assistance: Emergency Accommodation Support to Crisis-Affected Populations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As per the 2023 Global Humanitarian Overview, an estimated 339 million people will require some form of humanitarian assistance and protection in 2023. Access to dignified accommodation has always been one of the pressing needs during displacement crises, including in emerging and protracted settings. In many contexts, accommodation options include collective shelters where privacy and safety, especially for women, girls, and vulnerable populations are a concern. The setting up of displacement sites poses additional protection, and environmental concerns. With the support of Airbnb.org, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) is providing rental assistance to those in need through the Airbnb Inc. network of local partners (hosts) providing rental properties that meet habitability standards; rental of non-congregate housing solutions (hotels, motels, etc.); or the provision of complementary rental financial assistance. This Airbnb.org grant is being used to provide access to short-term rental accommodation support to displaced populations in ongoing crises or emerging/sudden onset crises, including but not limited to earthquake-affected populations in T&#xFC;rkiye.</narrative>
  </description>
